1
00:06:21,428 --> 00:06:27,428
Everyone's favourite bee is back!

2
00:12:42,857 --> 00:12:48,857
Maya the Bee: The Golden Orb is a adventure, animation,
family film directed by Noel Cleary.

3
00:19:04,285 --> 00:19:10,285
When Maya, a headstrong little bee, and her best friend Willy, rescue an ant princess, they find themselves in the middle
of an epic bug battle that will take them to strange new worlds and test their friendship to its limits.

4
00:25:25,714 --> 00:25:31,714
Maya (voice), played by Coco Jack Gillies.

5
00:31:47,142 --> 00:31:53,142
Willy (voice), played by Benson Jack Anthony.

6
00:38:08,571 --> 00:38:14,571
Crawley / Additional voices (voice), played by Jimmy James Eaton.

7
00:44:30,000 --> 00:44:36,000
Miss Cassandra / Aphids (voice), played by Tess Meyer.

8
00:50:51,428 --> 00:50:57,428
Queen (voice), played by Justine Clarke.

9
00:57:12,857 --> 00:57:18,857
Colonel (voice), played by Cam Ralph.

10
01:03:34,285 --> 01:03:40,285
Maya the Bee: The Golden Orb (also called Maya the Bee 3: The Golden Orb) is a
2021 animated adventure comedy film directed by Noel Cleary.

11
01:09:55,714 --> 01:10:01,714
Loosely based on characters from the 1975 anime Maya the Honey Bee and the German children's book The Adventures of Maya the Bee by Waldemar Bonsels, the film is a sequel to
the 2018 film Maya the Bee: The Honey Games, and stars the original voice cast of Coco Jack Gillies, Benson Jack Anthony, Frances Berry and Christian Charisiou.

12
01:16:17,142 --> 01:16:23,142
The Golden Orb was originally scheduled to be released in Australia on 17 June 2020, but
due to the COVID-19 pandemic, the film was pushed back to 7 January 2021.

13
01:22:38,571 --> 01:22:44,571
The film explores themes of friendship,
anthropomorphism, european, 3d animation, cartoon bee.
